---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CityHome from '../components/CityHome.astro';
import { primaryCity } from '../lib/cities';

/* A page per city. The primary city already owns "/", so its /<slug> page
   carries a canonical pointing back at the root rather than competing with it. */
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const cities = await getCollection('cities');
  return cities.map(city => ({ params: { city: city.id }, props: { city } }));
}

const { city } = Astro.props;
const primary = await primaryCity();
const isPrimary = city.id === primary.id;
const isLive = city.data.status === 'live';

const days = (await getCollection('gamedays'))
  .filter(d => d.data.city.trim().toLowerCase() === city.id);
const pastHere = days.filter(d => d.data.status === 'past').length;
---
{isLive ? (
  <Base
    title={`Dice & Tale ${city.data.name}`}
    description={`Monthly tabletop RPG game days in ${city.data.name}. Eight tables at once, volunteer game masters, and a seat kept for people who have never played.`}
    canonical={isPrimary ? '/' : undefined}
  >
    <CityHome citySlug={city.id} cityName={city.data.name} since={city.data.since} />
  </Base>
) : (
  <Base
    title={`Dice & Tale in ${city.data.name}?`}
    description={`Dice & Tale does not run game days in ${city.data.name} yet. Here is what starting one takes, and how to be the person who does it.`}
  >
    <section class="head">
      <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Not running here yet</p>
        <h1>{city.data.name} is a maybe</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          There are no Dice &amp; Tale game days in {city.data.name}. We would like
          there to be, and that depends entirely on somebody there wanting to start one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule--double" />

    <section>
      <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
        <h2>What starting a city actually takes</h2>
        <p>
          Not much, and less than people expect. Berlin began with eighteen people
          in a café. What it needs is:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>One person who will pick a date.</strong> This is the whole job
            and the only irreplaceable part.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A room with tables.</strong> A bookshop, a board game café, a
            bar with a back room. Two tables is a game day. Eight came later.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Two or three game masters</strong> willing to run a one-shot for
            strangers. They do not need to have done it before.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Nothing else.</strong> Booking, the code of conduct, the safety
            tools, the way the schedule is published, the poster template — all of
            that already exists and is yours to use.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you would get</h2>
        <p>
          The name, the booking setup, the content warnings and safety tooling, and
          somebody in Berlin who has run this monthly since 2024 and will tell you
          honestly what went wrong the first six times.
        </p>
        <p>
          What you would not get is money. Nobody is paid anywhere, including in
          Berlin.
        </p>

        <h2>If that is you</h2>
        <p>
          {city.data.contact
            ? <>Write to <a href={`mailto:${city.data.contact}`}>{city.data.contact}</a>.</>
            : <>Write to us through the <a href="/join">contact on the join page</a> and say which city.</>}
          {' '}Tell us where you are and whether you have a room in mind. That is
          enough to start the conversation.
        </p>
        <p class="alt">
          In the meantime, <a href="/">the {primary.data.name} game days</a> are open
          to anyone who happens to be there, and <a href="/new">what actually happens</a>
          {' '}describes a day end to end if you want to see what you would be copying.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </Base>
)}

<style>
  .head { padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); }
  .prose h2 { margin: 2.4rem 0 0.9rem; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose ul { padding-left: 1.15rem; }
  .prose li { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .prose li::marker { color: var(--gold); }
  .alt { color: var(--ink-mute); font-style: italic; }
</style>
